[
    {
        "content": "<p>I can't seem to find any API in Mathlib for the following notions:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">BoundedOn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Bornology</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bornology</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">IsBounded</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">''</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bounded</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Bornology</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">BoundedOn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">univ</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Should there be support for them in Mathlib, similar to the support given to <code>Monotone</code> /  <code>MonotoneOn</code>, or <code>Continuous</code> / <code>ContinuousOn</code>, etc.?  This is a pretty basic notion in analysis.</p>",
        "id": 595662530,
        "sender_full_name": "Terence Tao",
        "timestamp": 1779050616
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><del>The 2nd one looks similar to <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=BoundedSpace#doc\">docs#BoundedSpace</a> (because of <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=boundedSpace_induced_iff#doc\">docs#boundedSpace_induced_iff</a> + <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Set.image_univ#doc\">docs#Set.image_univ</a>)</del><br>\nEdit: nvm the docs hide the <code>Bornology.induced</code> inside the statement of <code>boundedSpace_induced_iff</code></p>",
        "id": 595667833,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1779054577
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Not in terms of bornology, but there is <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/39432\">#39432</a> for <code>enorm</code></p>",
        "id": 595668179,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Doll",
        "timestamp": 1779054899
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I don't think there's a need to create APIs for these two notions. Once you open Bornology it is already very concise. I believe the standard way to state these two notions in mathlib right now is <code>IsBounded (range f)</code> and <code>IsBounded (f '' s)</code>, as you can see in <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/Topology/MetricSpace/Bounded.html#Metric.isBounded_range_iff\">Metric.isBounded_range_iff</a> and <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/Topology/MetricSpace/Bounded.html#Metric.isBounded_image_iff\">Metric.isBounded_image_iff</a>.</p>",
        "id": 595669032,
        "sender_full_name": "Yongxi Lin (Aaron)",
        "timestamp": 1779055578
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Continuous/Monotone are different in the sense there are no corresponding notions for the sets (continuous/monotone sets), but we do have bounded sets <span aria-label=\"melting face\" class=\"emoji emoji-1fae0\" role=\"img\" title=\"melting face\">:melting_face:</span></p>",
        "id": 595669147,
        "sender_full_name": "Yongxi Lin (Aaron)",
        "timestamp": 1779055692
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The problem with that is the automation: you can't tag <code>IsBounded</code> with <code>fun_prop</code> because it does not involve any function argument, so you would have to rely on a discharger for that (I haven't done any experiments myself, but I have gotten the impression that <code>grind</code> does not play well with functions, but it might be worthwhile investigating that in the case when one only cares about the range)</p>",
        "id": 595675535,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Doll",
        "timestamp": 1779060617
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>No, I agree, these predicates should exist and I have wanted them in the past. I suggest <code>IsBddFun</code>/<code>IsBddFunOn</code>. I am not sure <code>IsBddFun</code> is necessary as opposed to using <code>IsBddFunOn .univ</code>.</p>",
        "id": 595715336,
        "sender_full_name": "Yaël Dillies",
        "timestamp": 1779080849
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>These can probably be <code>abbrevs</code>, right?</p>",
        "id": 595737338,
        "sender_full_name": "Edward van de Meent",
        "timestamp": 1779089593
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I don't think <code>abrev</code>s will work with <code>fun_prop</code>, though. IIRC, I tried that when introducing <code>HasFiniteMulSupport</code>/<code>HasFiniteSupport</code> a couple months ago (this was done to enable <code>fun_prop</code> to reason about functions having finite (multiplicative) support, similar to the motivation here).</p>",
        "id": 595767561,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Stoll",
        "timestamp": 1779097359
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>They shouldn't be abbrevs, no</p>",
        "id": 595789365,
        "sender_full_name": "Yaël Dillies",
        "timestamp": 1779102958
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>An annoying issue is the fact that integrability (the main motivation for <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/39432\">#39432</a>) uses enorms, and any ENNReal function/set is bounded in the bornology sense.</p>",
        "id": 595811644,
        "sender_full_name": "David Ledvinka",
        "timestamp": 1779108368
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I agree that this (<code>IsBddFunOn</code>) is currently a gap in the library, especially for the purposes of making automation play nice, but also for human interaction.</p>",
        "id": 595857495,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1779118061
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Heads up that I will soon PR some API for bounded function to mathlib</p>",
        "id": 602140782,
        "sender_full_name": "Yaël Dillies",
        "timestamp": 1781181972
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Why <code>IsBddFun</code>and not <code>Function.IsBounded</code>?</p>",
        "id": 602245067,
        "sender_full_name": "Antoine Chambert-Loir",
        "timestamp": 1781200674
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>... because this is primarily a statement about bornological spaces, not about functions. Certainly we don't want all function properties to be in the <code>Function</code> namespace!</p>",
        "id": 602245790,
        "sender_full_name": "Yaël Dillies",
        "timestamp": 1781200809
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>So <code>Bornology.IsBoundedFun</code>?</p>",
        "id": 602246596,
        "sender_full_name": "Antoine Chambert-Loir",
        "timestamp": 1781200950
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><code>Bornology.IsBddFun</code> actually, since the shortening is standard and already used in mathlib</p>",
        "id": 602259357,
        "sender_full_name": "Yaël Dillies",
        "timestamp": 1781203533
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'm aware <code>BddAbove</code> and <code>BddBelow</code> exist, but I still think <code>Bornology.IsBoundedFun</code> is clearer and more readable here</p>",
        "id": 602261281,
        "sender_full_name": "Bhavik Mehta",
        "timestamp": 1781203909
    }
